        <h2 id="top-10">Top 10 Embroidered Hoodie Manufacturers in China (2026 List)</h2>
        <p>The ten below are grouped by strength, each in the same format so you can compare them line by line. MOQ and lead-time figures reflect typical terms for programs of this type; real numbers move with season, fabric availability, and order mix, so confirm current terms directly with each supplier before you build them into a plan.</p>
        <h3>1. YAUUM: Best for Embroidery-Led Custom Programs</h3>
        <p><strong>Company Overview</strong></p>
        <p>YAUUM is a B2B menswear manufacturer across six categories: hoodies, T-shirts, jackets, pants, sportswear, and streetwear, positioned on process depth rather than catalog breadth, with embroidery run in-house instead of subcontracted.</p>
        <p><strong>Embroidery Capabilities &amp; Specialties</strong></p>
        <p>Flat embroidery, 3D puff, chenille, and applique, with placements on chest, back, sleeve, cuff, hem, and pocket edge. High-detail or large-format artwork goes through a strike-off before bulk release, which remains the single most reliable way to catch density and registration faults while they still cost nothing. To see the technique range in person, <a href="/hoodie-manufacturer/#decoration">explore our embroidery capabilities</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>MOQ, Lead Time &amp; Sampling</strong></p>
        <p>300–500 pieces per color on custom embroidered hoodies. Sampling runs 7–15 days, bulk production 30–45 days, plus 25–35 days on the water to most US and EU ports.</p>
        <p><strong>Who It's Best For</strong></p>
        <p>Brands that judge a supplier on embroidery fidelity, want OEM or private-label control, and would rather hear why a stitch spec works than receive a price with no reasoning attached.</p>
